WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.130
- [Instructor] So we have the graph here

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.570
of Y is equal to P of x,

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:08.140
I could write it like
this, Y is equal to P of x.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.970
And they say, what is the remainder

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:14.120
when P of x is divided by x plus three?

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.370
So pause this video and see
if you can have a go at this

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.180
and they tell us your
answer should be an integer.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.090
So, as you might have assumed,

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.500
this will involve the
polynomial remainder theorem

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.960
and all that tells us is that
hey if we were to take P of x

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.723
and divide it by x plus three,

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.000
whatever the remainder is here,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.600
so we'll say the remainder is equal to k.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.740
That value k is what we would have gotten

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.620
if we took our polynomial

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:46.210
and we evaluated it at the value of x

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.760
that would have made x
plus three equal zero

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.760
or just what would have happened

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.400
if I evaluated our polynomial
as x equals negative three.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.610
You have to be very careful there

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:56.950
sometimes people get confused.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.240
They see a positive three

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.010
and then they evaluate the
polynomial at the positive three

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:01.850
to figure out the remainder.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:02.683
No!

00:01:02.683 --> 00:01:03.910
If you saw a positive three there,

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:06.350
you would evaluate the
polynomial at negative three

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:10.700
but this should be equal to k as well.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.930
And so what is the remainder when P of x

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.699
is divided by x plus three?

00:01:15.699 --> 00:01:20.260
Well it's going to be equal
to P of negative three.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.920
P of negative three it looks like

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.760
it is equal to negative two.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.070
It is equal to negative
two, so our remainder

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:30.510
is equal to negative
two in this situation.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.350
Let's do another example,

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:35.040
actually let's do several more examples.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.060
Here we're told that P of x is
equal to all of this business

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:42.590
where k is an unknown
integer, very interesting.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:47.270
P of x divided by x minus
two has a remainder of one.

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:49.290
What is the value of k?

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.700
So pause this video again,
see if you can work it out.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.230
All right, well this second sentence

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.930
that P of x divided by x minus
two has a remainder of one,

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:02.690
that tells us that P not of negative two

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:04.360
but P of positive two,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:07.530
whatever x value would make
this expression equal zero.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:10.090
That P of two is equal to one.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:12.460
And then we could use this top information

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.460
to figure out what P of two would be.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:17.400
It would be two to the fourth power

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.130
minus two times two to the third power

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:25.590
plus k times two squared.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:29.920
So, times two squared minus 11,

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.400
and so all of that, that's
P of two right over here

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.070
that's going to be equal to one.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.200
Two to the fourth is 16

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.750
and then two times two to the third

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:40.490
that's two to the fourth
again, so it's minus 16

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:45.490
plus four k minus 11 is equal
to one, these cancel out.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.710
Now let's see we can add 11
to both sides of this equation

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:54.710
and we get four k is equal to 12.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:59.950
Divide both sides by four and
we get k is equal to three

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.010
and we're done.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.130
Let's do another example,
in fact let's do two more

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:04.780
because we're having so much fun.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:11.230
So this next question tells
us, P of x is a polynomial

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:15.420
and they tell us what P of x
divide by various things are,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.760
what the remainder would
be when you divide P of x

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.540
by these various expressions.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.810
Find the following values of P of x,

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.300
P of negative four and P of one.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.900
Pause this video and see
if you can have a go at it.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.960
All right, so P of negative four,

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.610
this is going to be equal to the remainder

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:42.380
when P of x divided by what.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:46.200
You might be tempted to say x minus four

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.660
but they're trying to
trick you intentionally.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.350
This would be the remainder when P of x

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:53.480
is divided by x plus four.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:54.990
And so they tell us right over here

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:58.640
P of x divided by x plus four
has a remainder of three.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:00.270
So, it's going to be
three right over there.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:05.260
And similarly P of one, this
is going to be the remainder,

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:10.260
this is the remainder
when P of x divided by

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:14.650
not x plus one, but x minus one.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.880
So when P of x is divided by x minus one,

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.430
the remainder is zero.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.743
Let's do one last example.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:26.480
So once again P of x is a polynomial

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.940
and then they give us
a few values of P of x.

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.550
And they say what is the remainder

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:34.760
when P of x is divided by x minus three?

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.120
Pause the video and try
to think about that.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.040
Well, we've gone over this multiple times,

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.150
the remainder when P of x
is divided by x minus three

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:45.580
that would be P of not negative
three, P of positive three.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:50.210
Whatever value of x makes this
entire expression equal zero.

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:54.830
So P of positive three is equal to five.

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:56.730
And similarly what is the remainder,

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.450
actually not so similarly,
this is interesting.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:01.107
What is the remainder when
P of x is divided by x?

00:05:01.107 --> 00:05:02.030
I know what you're thinking

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:05.460
it's like wait what
number am I dealing with?

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.620
But if I were to rewrite this

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:07.840
instead of saying divided by x,

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:11.550
if I were to say divided by x plus zero

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.480
then you'd be like oh now I get it.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:17.809
Or if I wrote divided by x minus zero,

00:05:17.809 --> 00:05:19.524
you'd be like oh, now I get it.

00:05:19.524 --> 00:05:23.150
This is going to be P
of and it doesn't matter

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:25.240
whether I take a positive
or a negative zero,

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:26.960
it's going to be P of zero.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:31.073
And P of zero, they tell us,
is negative one and we're done.

